From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:48:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 42/42] wayland: let trusted clients manage the clipboard with
 ext-data-control-v1

Implement ext_data_control_manager_v1 for the clipboard and the primary
selection. Devices get the current selections when created and every
change after, offers read from any owner, and sources become the owner
until they are replaced or destroyed. Setting no source clears the
selection.

This lets password managers copy a password and clear it again later
without being focused. Clients that are not sandboxed can already read
the clipboard through Xwayland, so they get the global; Flatpak apps get
it only when their app ID is in com.lantharos.kestrel
clipboard-access-apps.
